---
description: Core invariants for the Aquatic Guardian repository
alwaysApply: true
---
Read AGENTS.md before making changes. Follow its single-sources-of-truth table and non-negotiable rules.

- Do not invent thresholds, coefficients, legal citations, dates or statuses. Use a named source or mark the value `placeholder` / `verify` and tell the user.
- Never loosen a test tolerance to get green. Find the cause in the equations or the data.
- After any change run `pytest -q` and `python app/build.py --check`. Report the result.
- Keep changes small and reviewable. Explain what you changed and why, and list anything a human expert still has to check.
- Update docs/VERIFICATION.md and CHANGELOG.md when behaviour changes.
